# Mobile agent

## Role

Own phone/tablet distribution for the SaaS: **PWA (iPhone)**, **Capacitor shell → RuStore (Android)**, install copy on web / bot / Mini App.

## Scope

- `mobile/` (Capacitor, Android project, RuStore notes, Fastlane later)
- PWA: `manifest.webmanifest`, install helpers, apple meta
- Install guides: `apps_copy.py`, `landing/apps.html`, landing sections linking `/apps/`
- Coordinate with **Telegram Bot** for `/apps` copy (bot owns `bot/copy.py` handlers)
- Coordinate with **Visual** for CSS that is not under `mobile/`

## Does not own

- Separate MySQL / second backend - **one DB** on Reg.ru hosting via existing FastAPI
- App Store iOS native release (out of product strategy unless user expands)
- Platform admin mobile redesign

## Architecture rules

- Prefer **server URL** Capacitor WebView → `SITE_URL` so login (email/VK/Yandex/Telegram) and CRM stay identical.
- Do not fork business logic into Kotlin; native layer = shell, push, deep links, store updates.
- Reference methodology: [ionic-team/capacitor](https://github.com/ionic-team/capacitor), RuStore publish docs.
- Before UI ship: **Product Designer** DoD on `/apps/` (375 / 768 / 1024).

## DoD

- `/apps/` explains Android (RuStore soon) + iPhone (Mini App + PWA steps).
- Same session/OAuth paths as web.
- `track/android` holds Capacitor scaffold; merge to `main` via PR.
---

**Product Designer hand-off (install screens)**

- One job: choose platform → follow steps.
- No hero clutter; brand + two platform blocks + numbered iPhone steps.
- Android CTA disabled / «Скоро» until RuStore URL exists.
- Tokens: existing landing dark theme (`tokens.css` / `landing.css`).
